{"version":"0.1.20260917","status_code":20000,"status_message":"Ok.","time":"6.1870 sec.","cost":0.00599,"tasks_count":1,"tasks_error":0,"tasks":[{"id":"09181824-2505-0612-0000-ae44dd5bac42","status_code":20000,"status_message":"Ok.","time":"6.0889 sec.","cost":0.00599,"result_count":1,"path":["v3","ai_optimization","perplexity","llm_responses","live"],"data":{"api":"ai_optimization","function":"llm_responses","se":"perplexity","user_prompt":"How do you make charts on a website visible without JavaScript?","model_name":"sonar","max_output_tokens":900,"temperature":0.2},"result":[{"model_name":"sonar","input_tokens":19,"output_tokens":371,"reasoning_tokens":0,"web_search":true,"money_spent":0.00539,"datetime":"2026-09-18 18:24:54 +00:00","items":[{"type":"message","sections":[{"type":"text","text":"To make charts visible **without JavaScript**, the most reliable approach is to render them with **HTML/CSS or SVG directly in the page markup**, or to serve a **static image fallback** in a `<noscript>` block or plain `<img>` tag.[1][2][8][11]\n\nCommon no-JS options are:\n\n- **SVG charts**: draw the chart in `<svg>` using shapes like `<path>`, `<polyline>`, `<circle>`, and `<text>`; SVG can be fully visible without script.[1][4][16]\n- **Pure CSS charts**: build bars, pies, or progress indicators with CSS features such as flexbox, gradients, or custom properties.[2][15][16]\n- **HTML table-based charts**: keep the data in a table and style it into a chart with CSS; this is also good for accessibility and fallback content.[5][7][10][18]\n- **Static image fallback**: generate a PNG or SVG server-side and display it with `<img>` or inside `<noscript>` for users with JavaScript disabled.[8][11]\n- **Server-side rendering of a chart**: create the chart on the server and send the finished SVG/PNG to the browser, so it appears immediately without client-side JavaScript.[11]\n\nIf you want the chart to be both visible and responsive without JS, SVG is usually the best choice because it scales well and can be styled with CSS.[1][4][16] If accessibility matters, include the underlying data in an HTML table or provide descriptive `alt` text for image fallbacks.[5][8][11]\n\nIf you want, I can show you a minimal **no-JavaScript bar chart example** using either **SVG** or **pure CSS**.","annotations":[{"title":"A new technique for making responsive, JavaScript-free charts","url":"https://dev.to/richharris/a-new-technique-for-making-responsive-javascript-free-charts-gmp","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Eye-Catching CSS Charts That Will Revamp Your Data Reporting","url":"https://www.sliderrevolution.com/resources/css-charts/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"HTML Charts Without JavaScript","url":"https://medium.com/@anywhichway/html-charts-without-javascript-760a6089bb91","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"SVG charts without JavaScript – Part 1","url":"https://claudiorimann.com/svg-charts-without-javascript-part-1/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Accessibility issues","url":"https://groups.google.com/g/google-visualization-api/c/CIWNxu8B1z8","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Javascript chart library with noscript fallback support","url":"https://softwarerecs.stackexchange.com/questions/73836/javascript-chart-library-with-noscript-fallback-support","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Eleventy","url":"https://www.roboleary.net/blog/eleventy-charts/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"I Used The Web For A Day With JavaScript Turned Off","url":"https://www.smashingmagazine.com/2018/05/using-the-web-with-javascript-turned-off/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Visualizing Figures Without Any Charts — JS Chart Tips","url":"https://www.anychart.com/blog/2024/09/23/figures-without-charts/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"making a bar chart only with HTML","url":"https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-html/2019May/0001.html","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Embedding Charts in Blogs and Websites - adagger","url":"https://www.adagger.com/blog/embedding-charts-in-blogs-and-websites/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Chart.js","url":"https://www.chartjs.org/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"SVG Animated Chart without JavaScript, is it possible? - SitePoint","url":"https://www.sitepoint.com/community/t/svg-animated-chart-without-javascript-is-it-possible/224689","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"HTML Charts Without JavaScript","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/stories/118668/html-charts-without-javascript","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Creating Bar Charts Using Only HTML5 and CSS3","url":"https://ranaldo.co.uk/blog/posts/creating-bar-charts-using-only-html5-and-css3.html","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Three ways to draw pie charts without any JavaScript - Rainforest QA","url":"https://www.rainforestqa.com/blog/drawing-pie-charts-without-javascript","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Is possible to make working data charts using only plain html, css, js?","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/webdev/comments/1orxadj/is_possible_to_make_working_data_charts_using/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Using the Web for a Day with JavaScript Turned Off","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=17020688","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null},{"title":"Understanding Web Crawlers: Traditional vs. OpenAI's Bots","url":"https://prerender.io/blog/understanding-web-crawlers-traditional-ai/","start_index":null,"end_index":null,"text":null}]}]}],"fan_out_queries":null}]}]}